                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Boy Next Door is a crude, endless runner parody game based on \"Gachimuchi\" internet memes where you control a character named Van who must dodge gays and bodybuilders and collect vodka bottles to reach a club\n\nThis isn't even a game, let alone a fun game. This is basically human slop - before AI slops, we had human slops; there is no gameplay value here—it is a broken, repetitive runner that often cannot be played fairly due to poor coding; I've heard that there're instances, where the game generates impossible-to-dodge obstacles, making completing levels impossible for that instance, but fortunately, I haven't encountered any of them.",
